  "summary": "Nick Xenophon Team (NXT) senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after discovering she held British citizenship by descent through her mother, making her ineligible under dual-citizenship rules. She received confirmation from the UK Home Office on Friday, verified by a specialist barrister. Her mother, born in Singapore in 1957 (then a British colony), became a British citizen in 1983 under the British Nationality Act, passing that citizenship to Kakoschke-Moore, who was born in Darwin in 1985. Kakoschke-Moore said she was 'heartbroken' and surprised by the discovery, as her father had previously been advised by the British embassy in Oman that she was not eligible for citizenship when she was 12. She intends to request that the matter be referred to the high court to determine how her vacancy should be filled and hopes to return to the Senate in the future. A recount of the 2016 Senate election would likely elect NXT candidate Tim Storrer, though Nick Xenophon said preliminary legal advice suggests the seat may not be filled by recount, describing the situation as 'uncharted legal territory' following the high court's recent ruling on Hollie Hughes. Xenophon expressed devastation at the loss but predicted it was not the end of Kakoschke-Moore's political career."
}
